tier1-routes.txt.gz

A full Internet routing table, ~1,062,046 prefixes with the prefix-length
distribution a real ISP sees — 537,698 /24s in IPv4 alone.

From github.com/gaissmai/iprbench (MIT, Copyright (c) 2024 gaissmai), the
benchmark suite of bart's author. Redistributed here under that licence.

It is committed for a reason the provider corpora cannot serve: those are
fetched by fetch.sh and drift, and a licensed commercial database cannot be
committed at all, so figures taken from either are not reproducible by a
reader. This one is fixed and public, so the numbers derived from it can be
checked.

It is also the shape least favourable to this package. Provider allocations
barely nest; a routing table is announcements inside announcements, which is
what bart is built for. Measuring here rather than only on the corpora that
flatter the design is the point of having it.
